------------------------------------------------------------------------
*             OVERNIGHT AND FOUR-HOUR LETTERS
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Delivery on Weekends and Holidays:
 
Paper copy messages posted on weekends or holidays are treated as if
posted at 8:00 AM the next business day; that is, an Overnight Letter
posted on Sunday afternoon will be treated as if you posted it Monday at
8:00 AM, and will be delivered by noon on Tuesday.
------------------------------------------------------------------------
MCI MAIL CANNOT deliver Overnight or Four-Hour Letters without:
 
o  A correct ZIP CODE at the end of the last address line
o  A street address, not a P.O. Box
o  Someone present at the destination to receive your MCI Letter
------------------------------------------------------------------------
Type HELP <state> for a list of the zip codes in a particular state to
which you can send a 4HOUR or ONITE Letter; for example:
 
HELP NEWJERSEY    or    HELP NDAKOTA      or      HELP WASHINGTONDC
 
Press RETURN for more; type NO to stop:

------------------------------------------------------------------------
FOUR-HOUR Letters must be posted by 6:00 PM recipient's time, Monday
through Friday (excluding holidays), to be delivered within four hours.
Four-Hour Letters posted after 6:00 PM recipient's time will be
delivered by 10:00 AM the next business day.
------------------------------------------------------------------------
OVERNIGHT Letters must be posted by 5:00 PM sender's time, Monday
through Friday (excluding holidays), to be delivered by noon the next
business day.
------------------------------------------------------------------------
*               SIGNATURE/LETTERHEAD GRAPHICS
------------------------------------------------------------------------
To use your default signature graphic:
 
Type  /SIGNED/  in the leftmost position of the line of text on which
you wish your signature to appear.
------------------------------------------------------------------------
To request a signature other than your default:
 
Type  /SIGNED/ in the leftmost position of the line of text on which you
wish your signature to appear; then, in response to the "Handling:"
 
Press RETURN for more; type NO to stop:

prompt type SIGN: followed by the registered name of your graphic; e.g.,
 
Handling:  SIGN:PERSONALSIG
------------------------------------------------------------------------
To request a letterhead other than your default:
 
In response to the "Handling:" prompt, type FORM: followed by the
registered name of your graphic; e.g.,
 
Handling:  FORM:PARTNERLOGO
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
To obtain a Signature/Letterhead Registration form, send a message
TO:  MCIHELP .
------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                    MESSAGE FORMAT GUIDELINES
------------------------------------------------------------------------
PRESS RETURN AFTER EVERY LINE YOU TYPE.
Some devices are capable of "wrapping" input as you type.  But MCI Mail
requires a "hard" carriage return after every line of text.  We
recommend that your lines not be longer than 80 characters, and that you
press the RETURN key after every line.
 
Press RETURN for more; type NO to stop:

------------------------------------------------------------------------
USE CONTROL-L TO FORCE PAGINATION.
In the TEXT of your message, hold down the CONTROL key and press L to
force the subsequent text onto a new page when it is laser-printed.
(Note that CONTROL-L does NOT affect electronic copies of the message.)
------------------------------------------------------------------------
LASER-PRINTED PAGES ARE MAXIMUM 80 CHARACTERS WIDE, 54 LINES LONG.
The actual number of lines of text that appears on the first page of
your printed letter will vary, depending on the number of lines required
for the letterhead graphic (MCI Mail graphic uses 10 lines), and the
number of lines used for the recipient's postal address (maximum 5).
------------------------------------------------------------------------
*                        PRICING
------------------------------------------------------------------------
The "MCI Mail Ounce" is measured as 7500 characters for electronic
copies, or 3 pages (excluding the address page) for printed copies.  The
prices below reflect the cost for the first "Ounce"; an additional
"Ounce" costs $1.00, no matter which delivery option you choose:
 
Instant Letter:    delivered instantly to recipient's MCI Mailbox  $1.00
MCI Letter:        delivered via First Class U.S. Mail             $2.00
 
Press RETURN for more; type NO to stop:

Overnight Letter:  hand-delivered by noon next business day        $6.00
Four-Hour Letter:  hand-delivered within 4 hours the same day     $25.00
------------------------------------------------------------------------
 
 
 
